Package: ezekiel
Type: Package
Title: A Friendly Toolkit for Working with SQL Server
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Geordie", "McRuer", , "geo.mcruer@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Wraps 'RODBC' in consistent, pipe-friendly ezql_* functions so that SQL
    Server work feels like working with data frames: stored connection details,
    reading and writing tables, keeping a table in sync with a data frame,
    managing columns through a central name and type mapping (the rosetta),
    querying system-versioned (temporal) history as of any date, and making
    audited corrections with ezql_fix(). Every database read and write in 'tina'
    goes through it.
